    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa has been looking kinda rough lately. some of the lower leaves are turning a weird yellowish color and they feel a bit soft. i think i've been watering it about once a week but i'm not sure if that's too much or if it just needs more food? any idea what's going on?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing lower leaves that feel soft are likely signs of overwatering or root rot rather than a nutrient deficiency, as monstera plants typically yellow from above when they need food. Since watering once a week feels frequent for many monstera varieties, try letting the soil dry out completely before watering again to stress the roots lightly. If you want to replenish nutrients, apply a diluted, slow-release houseplant fertilizer once the plant recovers from the watering issue.",
