      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that \"unseen force\" you feel is almost certainly soil-borne pathogens like payday fungi (pythium) or other root rots that spread quickly through the wet soil. While these fungi aren't parasites that \"consume\" the plant like pests, they actively destroy the roots' ability to absorb water and nutrients, causing the rapid decline you see. To stop the spread immediately, you'll need to carefully remove the affected plant from its pot and trim away any brown, mushy roots before repotting it in fresh, sterile soil with better drainage to prevent reinfestation.",
